WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.310
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:08.580 --> 00:10.615
JULY 27, 2:00 P.M.

3
00:35.507 --> 00:37.842
The lightning is getting closer, right?

4
00:37.909 --> 00:39.844
Let's find a safe place to wait this out.

5
00:39.911 --> 00:41.146
Yes!

6
00:42.780 --> 00:44.048
So cold.

7
00:48.186 --> 00:50.955
I'll boil some water now, Mr. Nikaido.

8
00:54.425 --> 00:56.794
Mr. Nikaido, keep your stance low.

9
00:56.861 --> 00:58.129
Crouch down!

10
00:58.196 --> 01:00.565
I can't get any reception.

11
01:00.632 --> 01:02.333
Well yeah, we're in the mountains.

12
01:02.400 --> 01:04.736
-They told you to sit… -Shut up! You're always…

13
01:04.802 --> 01:05.803
So close!

14
01:05.870 --> 01:07.405
Too close! This is bad!

15
01:07.972 --> 01:08.940
Crouch down low.

16
01:09.007 --> 01:10.909
-Calm down. -Remain calm.

17
01:10.975 --> 01:13.044
Calm down and don't move.

18
01:13.111 --> 01:16.481
My fingers feel all prickly.

19
01:17.549 --> 01:18.750
Cover your ears!

20
01:32.063 --> 01:33.598
During disasters…

21
01:34.632 --> 01:38.303
After three days, chances of survival drastically drop.

22
01:39.037 --> 01:42.340
We refer to them as, "The critical 72 hours"

23
01:42.407 --> 01:44.976
and they are an important guideline for rescuers.

24
01:47.212 --> 01:48.313
Nono…

25
01:49.047 --> 01:50.248
Nono…

26
01:50.882 --> 01:51.849
Nono…

27
02:17.208 --> 02:18.209
Mr. Awashima?

28
02:18.276 --> 02:19.777
Did you get some sleep, Ogoma?

29
02:20.712 --> 02:22.547
Was anyone found?

30
02:22.614 --> 02:25.350
No. All six of them are still missing.

31
02:25.984 --> 02:28.319
At dawn, the rescue team will enter the mountain.

32
02:28.853 --> 02:30.255
I have a bad feeling.

33
02:30.321 --> 02:32.624
-Could you come to the scene early? -Got it.

34
02:36.361 --> 02:38.563
Okay, all set.

35
02:50.875 --> 02:56.281
SHIKARA POLICE STATION

36
02:56.347 --> 02:58.549
Please be careful.

37
02:58.616 --> 03:00.084
On to the next news.

38
03:00.151 --> 03:02.720
At Mount Shikara in Shikara Town, Hokkaido,

39
03:02.787 --> 03:06.424
six hikers are still missing.

40
03:07.091 --> 03:10.528
They were scheduled to descend the mountain yesterday afternoon.

41
03:10.595 --> 03:12.397
However, contact was lost,

42
03:12.930 --> 03:16.267
and the tour company reported to the police

43
03:16.334 --> 03:19.971
that five mountain tour participants and one guide had not returned.

44
03:20.038 --> 03:23.141
The police believe that the six are lost in the mountain

45
03:23.207 --> 03:26.644
and plan to begin search operations at dawn.

46
03:29.681 --> 03:34.385
Among the missing are…

47
04:10.822 --> 04:13.391
I will explain the search plan.

48
04:13.458 --> 04:16.227
Search teams one to three will search the eastern stream.

49
04:16.294 --> 04:17.295
Yes!

50
04:17.362 --> 04:19.731
Paramedic teams one and two will search the southern ridge,

51
04:19.797 --> 04:23.968
the area near the summit and the forest, and along the cliff…

52
04:28.506 --> 04:29.640
Mr. Awashima.

53
04:29.707 --> 04:31.409
Memorize the document.

54
04:31.476 --> 04:32.410
Okay.

55
04:34.746 --> 04:36.948
Did you get in touch with their families?

56
04:37.014 --> 04:38.750
They are waiting at their homes.

57
04:40.218 --> 04:42.620
Do we know what the missing hikers were wearing?

58
04:42.687 --> 04:46.124
No, we also have no eyewitnesses. The mountain doesn't have much to offer.

59
04:46.991 --> 04:49.694
They had a guide called Ms. Tabatake with them, right?

60
04:49.761 --> 04:51.696
So they are not all experienced hikers.

61
04:51.763 --> 04:53.398
I have a bad feeling.

62
04:53.464 --> 04:55.967
It's only been half a day.

63
04:57.068 --> 04:59.804
Last night in the mountains, it dropped to eight degrees.

64
04:59.871 --> 05:02.473
I'll go over the names of the six to be rescued.

65
05:02.540 --> 05:04.776
The guide, Ms. Motoka Tabatake.

66
05:04.842 --> 05:07.745
Mr. Ryutaro Monden, Mrs. Misaki Monden, a married couple.

67
05:07.812 --> 05:09.547
-Mr. Teruyuki Nikaido. -Yes.

68
05:09.614 --> 05:11.182
-Ms. Aya Saruwatari. -Yes.

69
05:11.249 --> 05:12.683
-Mr. Hitoshi Uematsu. -Yes.

70
05:12.750 --> 05:14.852
-That is all. -Aya Saruwatari…

71
05:14.919 --> 05:16.254
AYA SARUWATARI (38)

72
05:16.320 --> 05:17.989
-Let's depart! -Yes!

73
05:22.093 --> 05:23.828
I hope they are all found safe.

74
05:24.762 --> 05:27.131
Search operations are currently ongoing…

75
05:27.198 --> 05:28.499
Are you feeling all right?

76
05:29.834 --> 05:31.102
Everything looks all right.

77
05:31.169 --> 05:32.703
Her condition is stable.

78
05:33.237 --> 05:35.606
Nono, did you eat breakfast?

79
05:35.673 --> 05:40.011
The tour company contacted the police, reporting a missing guide.

80
05:40.077 --> 05:42.780
According to police, the six are believed to have gotten lost,

81
05:42.847 --> 05:45.082
and their whereabouts remain unknown.

82
05:45.149 --> 05:46.184
Since yesterday afternoon…

83
05:46.250 --> 05:47.885
Good morning.

84
05:49.921 --> 05:51.889
Yes, this is Shikara Police Station.

85
05:51.956 --> 05:55.293
Hello, this is Yoshino from Doto General Hospital.

86
05:55.359 --> 05:58.763
I would like to inquire about the mountain accident on Mount Shikara.

87
05:59.630 --> 06:02.700
Ms. Nono Tabatake, who is hospitalized at our hospital,

88
06:02.767 --> 06:07.438
is worried because she cannot get in touch with her mother, Ms. Motoka Tabatake.

89
06:07.505 --> 06:10.374
I'll transfer you to the corresponding department. Please wait a moment.

90
06:17.181 --> 06:19.750
-Drone team to base. -Base to drone team, go ahead.

91
06:19.817 --> 06:23.888
Elevation 780 meters, off to the west side from Mount Shikara's ridge trail.

92
06:23.955 --> 06:28.459
On the southeastern slope below the cliff, we spotted a person in white clothing.

93
06:28.526 --> 06:29.460
Copy that.

94
06:31.596 --> 06:34.565
Paramedics to base. We have made contact.

95
06:34.632 --> 06:36.934
A male, believed to be in his 40s.

96
06:38.402 --> 06:40.271
Level 300, rigor mortis present.

97
06:40.338 --> 06:41.939
Suffered trauma to the head.

98
06:42.440 --> 06:44.709
It's our turn. Let's go.

99
06:45.276 --> 06:46.110
Okay.

100
06:48.913 --> 06:52.116
HOKKAIDO POLICE

101
07:05.696 --> 07:06.864
Your pace is too fast!

102
07:07.532 --> 07:09.233
-Ogoma! -This is nothing!

103
07:09.300 --> 07:10.501
Watch your step.

104
07:10.568 --> 07:11.402
Yes.

105
07:12.837 --> 07:14.305
Hey, don't run!

106
07:19.176 --> 07:20.745
Hey!

107
07:20.811 --> 07:22.380
Can you hear us?

108
07:22.446 --> 07:23.915
Mr. Nikaido?

109
07:23.981 --> 07:25.983
Ms. Saruwatari!

110
07:26.050 --> 07:27.785
Is anyone there?

111
07:27.852 --> 07:29.854
Hey!

112
07:31.656 --> 07:33.024
He fell from over there?

113
07:33.090 --> 07:33.925
Yes.

114
07:33.991 --> 07:35.793
He was way off the mountain trail.

115
07:35.860 --> 07:38.396
He probably couldn't see ahead because of the branches and grass.

116
07:38.462 --> 07:40.264
-Any others? -No, he's alone.

117
07:40.331 --> 07:42.366
Why did he get separated from the group?

118
07:42.433 --> 07:44.435
He was wearing just a short-sleeved T-shirt.

119
07:44.502 --> 07:46.304
Rain gear… this isn't his own.

120
07:46.370 --> 07:48.839
Why was he acting alone, dressed like this?

121
07:48.906 --> 07:51.442
Why did a beginner stray from the guide?

122
07:51.509 --> 07:55.112
-Don't just ask questions. Think-- -I'm thinking as I talk.

123
07:55.179 --> 07:56.113
Go ahead.

124
07:57.949 --> 08:00.751
Did he hit his head as he fell?

125
08:20.037 --> 08:20.938
Hey.

126
08:23.074 --> 08:23.908
I'm fine.

127
08:25.209 --> 08:26.877
What is the time of death?

128
08:26.944 --> 08:29.914
We'll conduct a detailed autopsy once we get down the mountain…

129
08:29.981 --> 08:31.248
Just a rough estimate.

130
08:31.882 --> 08:35.419
He likely passed away yesterday between 3:00 p.m. and 6:00 p.m.

131
08:45.630 --> 08:48.199
It got pretty cold in the mountain yesterday.

132
08:48.766 --> 08:52.903
He might have developed hypothermia, lost consciousness and fell.

133
08:55.906 --> 08:57.908
Let's request a post-mortem autopsy.

134
08:59.276 --> 09:00.978
I want some kind of clue.

135
09:01.512 --> 09:04.882
Search team six reporting back. We found a driver's license among his belongings.

136
09:04.949 --> 09:07.018
The victim is believed to be Mr. Teruyuki Nikaido.

137
09:09.020 --> 09:10.287
Watch your steps.

138
09:12.089 --> 09:14.191
-Yes? -This is the Shikara Police Station.

139
09:14.258 --> 09:15.226
The police?

140
09:15.292 --> 09:17.328
Are you Mrs. Harune Nikaido?

141
09:19.130 --> 09:19.964
Yes.

142
09:20.531 --> 09:22.400
We regret to inform you

143
09:22.466 --> 09:26.070
that your husband, Mr. Teruyuki, passed away on Mount Shikara.

144
09:28.272 --> 09:29.607
He died?

145
09:29.674 --> 09:31.709
LIFE INSURANCE

146
09:31.776 --> 09:34.211
-It's uneven here. Please be careful. -Yes.

147
09:34.278 --> 09:37.815
HOKKAIDO POLICE

148
09:37.882 --> 09:38.916
Okay.

149
09:39.483 --> 09:41.485
48 HOURS LEFT

150
09:41.986 --> 09:45.222
Huh? His body was just found, wasn't it?

151
09:45.289 --> 09:46.223
Yes, and yet

152
09:46.290 --> 09:50.127
the insurance company already received an inquiry about his life insurance.

153
09:50.928 --> 09:54.665
What a calm and composed wife.

154
09:54.732 --> 09:56.467
She is a strange one.

155
09:57.268 --> 09:58.502
How much is the payout?

156
09:58.569 --> 10:00.538
150 million yen.

157
10:00.604 --> 10:01.639
Oh wow.

158
10:01.706 --> 10:04.375
The contract was originally for 50 million yen,

159
10:04.442 --> 10:06.510
but they suddenly increased it two months ago.

160
10:06.577 --> 10:08.279
Well, well.

161
10:08.345 --> 10:09.413
I sent over the details.

162
10:09.480 --> 10:10.314
Read them to me.

163
10:10.381 --> 10:11.582
Read them yourself.

164
10:11.649 --> 10:13.050
I'm driving right now.

165
10:15.319 --> 10:18.456
The insured is Mr. Teruyuki Nikaido, 44 years old.

166
10:18.522 --> 10:21.158
He ran a restaurant in Asahikawa.

167
10:21.225 --> 10:24.061
The beneficiary is his wife, Ms. Harune, 58 years old.

168
10:24.128 --> 10:25.963
A 14-year difference? Any children?

169
10:26.030 --> 10:26.964
No.

170
10:27.031 --> 10:29.800
Harune will receive it all by herself.

171
10:30.501 --> 10:33.070
An older wife receiving 150 million yen, huh.

172
10:33.637 --> 10:35.539
I wonder what kind of person she is.

173
10:46.717 --> 10:48.586
Sounds fishy, huh. Are you listening?

174
10:48.652 --> 10:50.154
Yeah, I'm listening.

175
10:50.221 --> 10:52.523
It was a mountain accident, but schedule an appointment…

176
10:52.590 --> 10:53.724
Stop!

177
10:53.791 --> 10:54.458
Stop!

178
10:56.494 --> 10:57.862
The white minivan!

179
10:58.462 --> 10:59.897
Pull over to the left and stop!

180
10:59.964 --> 11:02.066
A red convertible escaping towards Abashiri…

181
11:02.133 --> 11:04.835
-Get out of the car. -The number plate is…

182
11:05.936 --> 11:07.838
Driver's license and car registration.

183
11:08.839 --> 11:11.742
Speeding violation, two penalty points.

184
11:11.809 --> 11:13.410
And a fine of 15,000 yen.

185
11:13.477 --> 11:15.813
Oh, I didn't realize I was over the limit.

186
11:15.880 --> 11:17.748
Please pay within eight days.

187
11:17.815 --> 11:20.017
-What about that red sports car? -My colleagues will handle it.

188
11:20.084 --> 11:22.419
There's no one around! Isn't this pointless?

189
11:22.486 --> 11:23.721
You still violated the law.

190
11:23.788 --> 11:25.623
You have an enforcement quota, don't you?

191
11:25.689 --> 11:27.625
-Nao. -I hate that part about you police.

192
11:27.691 --> 11:31.028
Only doing what the higher-ups tell you to…

193
11:31.095 --> 11:33.397
-Nao! That's not the way to go! -Here you go.

194
11:33.464 --> 11:34.865
What?

195
11:34.932 --> 11:36.767
Nao, don't pick a fight with them.

196
11:36.834 --> 11:39.703
In this job, we often rely on the police, you know.

197
11:39.770 --> 11:43.073
Don't you think it's them who have to rely on us,

198
11:43.140 --> 11:44.341
more often than not?

199
11:44.408 --> 11:46.410
Well, that's true too, but…

200
11:46.477 --> 11:49.613
Nao, smile.

201
11:54.919 --> 11:55.986
Hello.

202
12:06.864 --> 12:07.965
It's my husband…

203
12:38.262 --> 12:40.497
Must be tough for her, huh?

204
12:41.398 --> 12:45.069
Well, yeah. Her husband was fine until yesterday…

205
12:53.777 --> 12:54.979
What's wrong?

206
12:55.045 --> 12:57.381
She felt unwell.

207
12:57.448 --> 12:58.716
Would you like to sit down?

208
12:58.782 --> 12:59.917
Bathroom.

209
13:01.151 --> 13:02.419
Ms. Nikaido.

210
13:02.953 --> 13:04.822
How are you feeling?

211
13:06.123 --> 13:07.524
I'm fine.

212
13:38.489 --> 13:39.323
MISSING PERSONS LIST

213
13:39.390 --> 13:42.960
If we don't find them today, we check the north side tomorrow, I suppose.

214
13:43.027 --> 13:43.928
Yeah.

215
13:43.994 --> 13:47.231
Hello. Where is Ms. Harune Nikaido?

216
13:47.298 --> 13:48.465
Who might you be?

217
13:51.101 --> 13:52.069
Excuse me.

218
13:52.569 --> 13:53.804
She's busy right now.

219
13:53.871 --> 13:56.240
-Who are you? -Could you let me talk to her?

220
13:56.307 --> 13:57.341
Do it another day.

221
13:57.408 --> 13:59.209
Oh, my. I can't…

222
13:59.276 --> 14:01.345
We are way past our scheduled time.

223
14:01.412 --> 14:03.280
Ms. Nikaido, are you okay?

224
14:03.347 --> 14:05.082
Sorry for making you wait.

225
14:05.149 --> 14:07.551
You have my condolences.

226
14:12.122 --> 14:13.657
INVESTIGATOR - TSUKASA NAO

227
14:13.724 --> 14:14.558
"Choku…"

228
14:14.625 --> 14:16.694
It's Nao. Tsukasa Nao.

229
14:16.760 --> 14:18.395
I'm an insurance investigator.

230
14:18.462 --> 14:21.365
I need to ask a few questions about the late Mr. Teruyuki Nikaido's

231
14:21.432 --> 14:23.367
life insurance.

232
14:23.934 --> 14:25.536
An insurance investigator is here.

233
14:25.602 --> 14:27.004
Oh, for what?

234
14:27.071 --> 14:29.440
Something about life insurance.

235
14:29.506 --> 14:31.775
The body was only just found!

236
14:31.842 --> 14:33.811
Who is this guy?

237
14:35.980 --> 14:39.183
He's from Zennichi Insurance Research. Tsukasa Nao.

238
14:39.249 --> 14:41.151
Tsukasa Nao?

239
14:41.218 --> 14:43.187
He always acts so fast.

240
14:46.523 --> 14:47.992
Two months ago,

241
14:49.193 --> 14:52.830
the insurance contract was changed.

242
14:53.364 --> 14:55.366
Do you know why?

243
14:56.767 --> 14:57.701
I don't know.

244
14:59.036 --> 15:01.238
Did your husband often go mountain climbing?

245
15:01.739 --> 15:06.343
Yesterday, I thought he was playing golf with friends.

246
15:06.410 --> 15:10.280
So you don't usually know his plans?

247
15:10.881 --> 15:11.782
No.

248
15:12.483 --> 15:16.687
Why do you think he went to the mountains?

249
15:20.657 --> 15:21.925
You don't know?

250
15:23.060 --> 15:24.428
Were you two on good terms?

251
15:25.896 --> 15:26.797
We were normal.

252
15:26.864 --> 15:30.534
When did you last eat with Mr. Teruyuki?

253
15:30.601 --> 15:34.171
Dinner? Lunch? Breakfast?

254
15:35.372 --> 15:36.707
Can't you remember?

255
15:38.242 --> 15:40.144
-It's too sudden. She can't… -Hey, you.

256
15:40.210 --> 15:43.881
Let me change the question. Were you satisfied with your husband?

257
15:44.581 --> 15:48.986
Be it money-wise, emotionally, sexually… anything.

258
15:49.053 --> 15:51.055
-Hey. -You can choose not to answer.

259
15:51.121 --> 15:54.291
-Could you be quiet for a moment? -Did you have an appointment with him?

260
15:54.358 --> 15:55.926
What time was your appointment?

261
15:58.228 --> 16:00.397
I've never met him before.

262
16:00.464 --> 16:02.633
An appointment? Did I say I had one?

263
16:02.699 --> 16:04.768
-Please come with me. -Hey, what…

264
16:04.835 --> 16:06.437
-What? -Sorry.

265
16:06.503 --> 16:08.338
We are doing a police investigation here.

266
16:08.405 --> 16:10.741
I see. I got scolded by the police again.

267
16:10.808 --> 16:12.443
Why don't you choose your words better?

268
16:12.509 --> 16:15.012
You can't say that to someone who just lost family.

269
16:15.079 --> 16:16.080
What's wrong with it?

270
16:16.146 --> 16:18.582
I don't like how you pressured her so suddenly.

271
16:18.649 --> 16:20.517
I'm not working to impress you.

272
16:20.584 --> 16:22.486
-Passing through. -She's grieving!

273
16:22.553 --> 16:25.355
This is my job. In insurance, speed is everything.

274
16:25.422 --> 16:28.225
I'm racing against time too.

275
16:28.292 --> 16:30.994
I have five missing people. I want to get any clue I can.

276
16:31.061 --> 16:31.895
But…

277
16:32.396 --> 16:34.431
the family's feelings come first, got it?

278
16:34.498 --> 16:35.466
Are you…

279
16:36.066 --> 16:37.868
really a police officer?

280
16:38.469 --> 16:42.005
Don't the police think everyone is a thief?

281
16:42.072 --> 16:43.841
I've never thought that way.

282
16:43.907 --> 16:47.077
Are you a foolishly good man? Or a weakling who wants to look good?

283
16:47.144 --> 16:47.978
Which are you?

284
16:48.045 --> 16:49.213
What did you say?

285
16:49.780 --> 16:51.014
Too rough.

286
16:54.318 --> 16:55.452
Yes, what is it?

287
16:55.519 --> 16:57.287
-Found a hiker! -A missing hiker has been found.

288
16:58.455 --> 16:59.656
Who?

289
16:59.723 --> 17:02.426
Search team to headquarters. We found a hiker!

290
17:02.493 --> 17:03.660
Yeah!

291
17:03.727 --> 17:06.330
We believe it to be Ms. Tabatake.

292
17:08.599 --> 17:11.502
Ms. Motoka Tabatake, the guide. Ms. Aya Saruwatari, a hiker…

293
17:11.568 --> 17:12.569
Aya?

294
17:13.203 --> 17:14.037
Is she safe?

295
17:16.640 --> 17:18.976
Only Ms. Tabatake was found.

296
17:19.476 --> 17:21.612
-Ms. Tabatake, you okay? -Ten meters!

297
17:21.678 --> 17:23.680
-Ready for pickup! -Pulling up!

298
17:23.747 --> 17:25.382
-Pulling up! -Stand back.

299
17:25.449 --> 17:28.051
Going up! Stand back!

300
17:29.753 --> 17:32.055
She's unconscious. We're sending her over there.

301
17:34.224 --> 17:37.394
Nono. They found your mom.

302
17:39.329 --> 17:41.999
What about Ms. Saruwatari?

303
17:42.065 --> 17:43.267
Only her belongings.

304
17:46.003 --> 17:49.339
We found a hiking insurance application form in a stream, east side.

305
17:50.374 --> 17:51.341
A stream…

306
17:51.875 --> 17:53.277
So she came down the mountain?

307
17:53.343 --> 17:55.646
Maybe. We're searching the surrounding area carefully.

308
17:55.712 --> 17:56.547
Ogoma!

309
17:57.214 --> 17:58.315
They found a hiker!

310
17:58.882 --> 18:00.584
I just got back from a house call.

311
18:07.024 --> 18:08.425
Thank goodness.

312
18:09.326 --> 18:12.029
She's coming to this hospital now. You'll see her soon.

313
18:12.095 --> 18:13.430
Isn't that great, Nono?

314
18:13.497 --> 18:16.733
Thank goodness, huh.

315
18:16.800 --> 18:18.569
One of the missing?

316
18:20.504 --> 18:23.106
Nono's mom is a mountain guide.

317
18:23.173 --> 18:25.742
-Oh, Ms. Tabatake? -Yes!

318
18:25.809 --> 18:28.445
-I'm glad she was found. -Right?

319
18:28.512 --> 18:30.614
Nono has no father.

320
18:30.681 --> 18:34.184
If her mom disappeared too, I would be so worried.

321
18:34.251 --> 18:37.321
What is she being treated for?

322
18:37.387 --> 18:40.290
I don't know. Something with her immune system.

323
18:40.891 --> 18:42.025
-Thank you. -No problem.

324
18:47.231 --> 18:52.402
VISITOR PASS

325
18:54.605 --> 18:56.440
44 HOURS LEFT

326
18:57.608 --> 19:00.010
Search operations for all teams will end at sunset.

327
19:00.077 --> 19:02.613
Let's do our best to find the other four missing!

328
19:02.679 --> 19:04.348
If you can hear us, please answer!

329
19:04.414 --> 19:05.582
Ogoma.

330
19:08.018 --> 19:12.222
Tomorrow, we'll have more local rescue workers joining us

331
19:12.289 --> 19:14.024
to expand the search area.

332
19:14.091 --> 19:16.560
28 hours have already passed.

333
19:16.627 --> 19:18.528
Keep up the good work tomorrow!

334
19:28.071 --> 19:29.339
Hello.

335
19:29.406 --> 19:30.507
Hello.

336
19:41.351 --> 19:42.185
Hup.

337
19:44.521 --> 19:46.590
Your mom's body is exhausted.

338
19:46.657 --> 19:48.158
She's resting now.

339
19:49.159 --> 19:51.895
It will take time for her to wake up. Let's wait.

340
19:53.363 --> 19:55.032
Will she really wake up?

341
19:56.400 --> 19:57.467
It's okay.

342
19:58.468 --> 19:59.936
Your mom is strong.

343
20:11.782 --> 20:13.750
-Good job. -Good work today!

344
20:13.817 --> 20:15.886
Ms. Tabatake isn't doing well.

345
20:16.820 --> 20:20.357
She has severe hypothermia and blood loss, and is in the ICU.

346
20:20.424 --> 20:22.125
I hope she wakes up.

347
20:22.192 --> 20:23.093
Right?

348
20:23.160 --> 20:24.795
Four more people.

349
20:25.462 --> 20:28.832
Ms. Saruwatari, the Monden couple, and Mr. Uematsu.

350
20:28.899 --> 20:31.368
The families waiting for them have it rough too.

351
20:31.435 --> 20:33.136
Ms. Saruwatari…

352
20:33.203 --> 20:35.238
I might know her.

353
20:35.305 --> 20:36.306
Huh?

354
20:36.373 --> 20:38.542
It could be a person with the same name. I'm not sure.

355
20:38.608 --> 20:41.178
I hope they hold out.

356
20:41.244 --> 20:43.246
-Chief. -Huh?

357
20:43.313 --> 20:45.315
Can we really ignore that insurance investigator?

358
20:45.382 --> 20:46.216
Tsukasa Nao.

359
20:46.283 --> 20:47.584
Nao, Zennichi Insurance Research.

360
20:47.651 --> 20:50.387
That guy, he was at the response office too.

361
20:50.454 --> 20:53.757
He was asking everyone questions, as though he was part of the operation.

362
20:54.257 --> 20:55.525
What is he investigating?

363
20:56.126 --> 20:57.661
Teruyuki Nikaido.

364
20:57.728 --> 21:00.630
When an insured person gets hurt or dies,

365
21:00.697 --> 21:02.466
the insurance company pays money, right?

366
21:02.532 --> 21:06.336
-Yeah. -They don't always pay the full amount.

367
21:06.403 --> 21:09.573
They check if there is anything suspicious in the claim.

368
21:09.639 --> 21:11.041
Is he an insurance company employee?

369
21:11.108 --> 21:14.611
No. He works for a company that only does investigations.

370
21:15.545 --> 21:17.447
I heard he's very persistent.

371
21:17.514 --> 21:19.549
He's more insensitive than persistent.

372
21:20.183 --> 21:23.353
Remember the Hakodate fake family suicide case?

373
21:23.420 --> 21:25.522
The husband's mistress was the culprit.

374
21:25.589 --> 21:27.591
I wasn't born back then.

375
21:27.657 --> 21:30.193
You were born and at the police academy.

376
21:31.194 --> 21:33.029
Nao investigated the insurance claim.

377
21:33.096 --> 21:37.100
He reported it as a murder to the police which led to it becoming a case.

378
21:37.167 --> 21:40.670
Why are we police losing to an insurance investigator?

379
21:40.737 --> 21:42.406
Don't lose, police!

380
21:42.472 --> 21:45.909
The police have to solve case after case.

381
21:46.510 --> 21:49.346
Well, not like lots of cases happen around here.

382
21:49.413 --> 21:52.349
Well, yeah, but…

383
21:52.983 --> 21:55.819
Insurance investigators spend lots of time on one case.

384
21:55.886 --> 21:58.155
They probably have a bigger budget too.

385
21:58.221 --> 22:01.758
He might be amazing. But I don't like him.

386
22:01.825 --> 22:04.194
He does help us out sometimes.

387
22:04.261 --> 22:06.630
So cooperate with him as much as you can.

388
22:07.764 --> 22:09.299
-Ogoma. -Yes?

389
22:09.366 --> 22:11.067
-You want a promotion, right? -I do.

390
22:11.134 --> 22:13.703
If you stay close to him, he might give you info.

391
22:13.770 --> 22:15.839
I prioritize rescuing people.

392
22:16.773 --> 22:20.744
Tomorrow, the fire brigade and the mountain club will join us.

393
22:22.212 --> 22:24.448
Let me go into the mountain too.

394
22:24.514 --> 22:26.283
Leave it to people who know the mountain.

395
22:26.349 --> 22:29.286
I've been on that mountain more than those outsiders have.

396
22:29.352 --> 22:31.087
We don't have enough people.

397
22:31.154 --> 22:32.689
So let me help out.

398
22:35.125 --> 22:36.426
I'll be back by three.

399
22:58.448 --> 23:00.217
Hey. Detective?

400
23:01.284 --> 23:03.553
How did you know where I live?

401
23:03.620 --> 23:04.788
Who told you?

402
23:05.455 --> 23:07.190
Huh? No.

403
23:07.724 --> 23:10.427
-My place is there. -Where?

404
23:11.261 --> 23:12.562
Right there.

405
23:13.363 --> 23:14.397
What?!

406
23:14.464 --> 23:15.632
I'm closing the door.

407
23:17.834 --> 23:18.869
Okay.

408
23:19.769 --> 23:20.904
Nobody lives there!

409
23:20.971 --> 23:24.541
I rented that empty room for this business trip.

410
23:24.608 --> 23:27.577
Rescue workers filled up all the other inns. Bye.

411
23:29.279 --> 23:31.882
Oh, by the way. Mr. Tanaka…

412
23:31.948 --> 23:33.216
That's not my name.

413
23:33.283 --> 23:34.951
I forgot your name.

414
23:35.018 --> 23:36.753
I haven't told you my name.

415
23:36.820 --> 23:39.289
I'm Nao from Zennichi Insurance Research.

416
23:40.023 --> 23:41.892
I'm Ogoma from the Shikara Police Station.

417
23:41.958 --> 23:43.193
-Mr. Ogoma. -Yes.

418
23:43.260 --> 23:44.561
Mr. Ogoma.

419
23:44.628 --> 23:45.595
Yes, that's me.

420
23:45.662 --> 23:47.831
Did you talk to Ms. Nikaido after that?

421
23:48.732 --> 23:50.500
Did you find out anything else?

422
23:50.567 --> 23:54.070
Ms. Nikaido fainted from anemia. Who do you think caused that?

423
23:55.972 --> 23:56.840
Who could it be?

424
23:56.907 --> 23:59.242
I know it's your job, but don't get in the way of the police.

425
23:59.309 --> 24:00.243
Of course.

426
24:02.078 --> 24:04.481
You plan to go into the mountain, don't you?

427
24:04.548 --> 24:05.549
Do I?

428
24:05.615 --> 24:08.351
Please don't go in on your own. You could go missing.

429
24:09.419 --> 24:12.389
I'll join as part of the mountain club. I'm good with mountains.

430
24:12.455 --> 24:14.257
Are you making that up?

431
24:15.559 --> 24:17.827
I was in the mountaineering club in college.

432
24:18.361 --> 24:21.898
I've also handled many mountain accident insurance cases.

433
24:25.201 --> 24:26.403
Is this real?

434
24:27.837 --> 24:28.738
Huh?

435
24:28.805 --> 24:30.206
You doubt me?

436
24:31.708 --> 24:33.610
You've looked suspicious since you got here.

437
24:33.677 --> 24:35.545
That's good!

438
24:36.179 --> 24:37.847
Doubt everything.

439
24:38.615 --> 24:39.282
Huh?

440
24:40.116 --> 24:43.286
Once you have doubted everything, what remains…

441
24:43.353 --> 24:44.821
is the truth.

442
24:48.892 --> 24:50.160
The truth about what?

443
24:50.994 --> 24:51.928
Good night.

444
25:02.472 --> 25:04.374
Day two of the search. Thank you, everyone.

445
25:04.441 --> 25:05.475
Let's do our best!

446
25:05.542 --> 25:08.111
Thank you to the fire brigade and the mountain club too.

447
25:08.712 --> 25:10.814
Four missing people remain!

448
25:10.880 --> 25:12.782
Let's find them today, no matter what.

449
25:12.849 --> 25:14.084
Yes!

450
25:15.352 --> 25:17.520
Let's give it our all!

451
25:17.587 --> 25:19.022
Let's set off.

452
25:21.358 --> 25:22.859
Shall we go?

453
25:22.926 --> 25:25.662
-Come on. -Let's do this.

454
25:27.464 --> 25:29.466
-Is anyone there? -Can you hear me?

455
25:34.604 --> 25:36.306
Mr. Monden!

456
25:38.775 --> 25:40.310
Is anyone there?

457
25:40.910 --> 25:42.345
Can you hear me?

458
25:44.080 --> 25:46.016
Have you ever climbed this mountain?

459
25:46.082 --> 25:47.150
Of course.

460
25:47.217 --> 25:50.420
I usually look for people who get stuck picking wild vegetables.

461
25:50.487 --> 25:52.589
A police detective has to do that?

462
25:52.656 --> 25:55.258
They make me do everything. I'm the lowest rank.

463
25:55.325 --> 25:57.827
-How many years have you been a detective? -That doesn't matter.

464
25:57.894 --> 26:00.263
I guess six, seven years?

465
26:00.330 --> 26:04.601
In Sapporo or Asahikawa, you would get big cases by now.

466
26:04.668 --> 26:05.769
Can you hear me?

467
26:05.835 --> 26:08.271
I won't stay at the bottom forever.

468
26:08.338 --> 26:10.206
Search team six to base.

469
26:10.273 --> 26:12.542
We'll go off-course to the southeast.

470
26:12.609 --> 26:13.977
Wait!

471
26:14.044 --> 26:16.980
Ms. Saruwatari's belongings were found at the stream, right?

472
26:17.047 --> 26:19.883
If she lost her way, Ms. Saruwatari would climb to the ridge.

473
26:20.684 --> 26:22.318
Does she know mountains well?

474
26:23.019 --> 26:26.356
Hey, you are the one who told me this mountain was risky!

475
26:30.126 --> 26:31.995
You look lame!

476
26:32.562 --> 26:34.064
Where are you having lunch?

477
26:38.001 --> 26:39.202
Hey, stop it!

478
26:39.269 --> 26:42.105
-Miss! -Join us!

479
26:42.172 --> 26:44.407
Sure, once I'm done with this.

480
26:44.474 --> 26:46.176
Ogoma, everyone has to go!

481
26:46.242 --> 26:47.744
Let's be in the same group.

482
26:47.811 --> 26:48.778
Sure.

483
26:51.948 --> 26:53.450
I'm not going.

484
26:54.017 --> 26:55.552
Let's invite Imai too.

485
26:55.618 --> 26:57.487
Sounds good.

486
27:04.627 --> 27:05.462
Ogoma.

487
27:07.797 --> 27:08.865
Ogoma.

488
27:10.233 --> 27:11.201
Good morning.

489
27:12.268 --> 27:15.038
Ogoma. Let's go to class.

490
27:19.943 --> 27:21.144
Ogoma.

491
27:21.211 --> 27:23.246
What are you doing? Come back.

492
27:23.780 --> 27:25.648
We'll take a break once we reach that peak.

493
27:25.715 --> 27:27.650
-Ogoma. -Yes!

494
27:27.717 --> 27:28.718
Over here.

495
27:39.796 --> 27:41.164
Is this the right way?

496
27:41.231 --> 27:44.134
Let me check. This is search team six to base.

497
27:44.200 --> 27:47.837
-We went off course… -Where is he going?

498
27:49.472 --> 27:51.407
-Can you hear me? -Ogoma.

499
27:51.474 --> 27:52.909
You have to stop soon.

500
27:54.644 --> 27:56.146
Got to find them by today.

501
27:56.212 --> 27:57.547
We'll run into bears here.

502
27:58.148 --> 27:59.649
If a bear shows up, I'll fight it.

503
27:59.716 --> 28:01.351
A brown bear? Are you serious?

504
28:01.417 --> 28:02.252
Yes.

505
28:02.819 --> 28:06.422
-Let's go back. This old man is tired. -It will be cold tonight.

506
28:06.489 --> 28:08.024
We must find them by today…

507
28:08.091 --> 28:08.958
Please answer…

508
28:09.025 --> 28:11.694
-Is anyone there? Can you hear me? -The critical 72 hours?

509
28:12.362 --> 28:13.229
Yeah.

510
28:13.997 --> 28:16.266
Is anyone there? Can you hear me?

511
28:16.332 --> 28:17.801
Let's take a break and think…

512
28:17.867 --> 28:18.768
Please answer!

513
28:18.835 --> 28:19.702
Can you hear me?

514
28:19.769 --> 28:21.905
-Ogoma. -Answer me!

515
28:21.971 --> 28:22.939
Hey!

516
28:25.108 --> 28:27.010
Break! Break time!

517
28:27.076 --> 28:30.914
Break time.

518
28:35.351 --> 28:36.853
Come on.

519
28:37.420 --> 28:38.555
You too, Ogoma.

520
28:38.621 --> 28:39.489
Here.

521
28:40.056 --> 28:40.890
Refuel.

522
28:48.331 --> 28:49.265
Thanks.

523
28:55.738 --> 28:59.242
You came to investigate Mr. Nikaido's life insurance, right?

524
29:00.076 --> 29:01.110
Yeah.

525
29:01.911 --> 29:05.315
I can't write my report without knowing what happened.

526
29:07.283 --> 29:09.686
You had a reason to press his wife so hard.

527
29:13.289 --> 29:15.758
Well, yeah. I did things by the book.

528
29:15.825 --> 29:18.094
There is no "book" here. You suspected her.

529
29:20.363 --> 29:21.431
Can't you tell me?

530
29:27.837 --> 29:29.172
Harune…

531
29:30.273 --> 29:36.179
filed a life insurance claim right after her husband's body was found.

532
29:37.547 --> 29:40.149
Before the death certificate was even issued.

533
29:40.683 --> 29:42.151
It's not issued yet, right?

534
29:42.819 --> 29:43.686
Yeah.

535
29:43.753 --> 29:45.421
We're waiting for the autopsy.

536
29:45.955 --> 29:47.056
How much is the insurance?

537
29:47.123 --> 29:48.391
150 million yen.

538
29:48.458 --> 29:50.426
It was increased two months ago.

539
29:52.028 --> 29:53.529
She has a reason to want it fast.

540
29:53.596 --> 29:56.332
She runs a restaurant and has many employees.

541
29:56.399 --> 29:59.235
Still, isn't that too fast?

542
30:00.003 --> 30:04.240
Usually, people don't view a dead body as a cash payout right away.

543
30:04.307 --> 30:06.743
So I want to know what happened.

544
30:09.979 --> 30:13.650
I want to hear from Mr. Nikaido's companions about why he died.

545
30:13.716 --> 30:14.651
You do too, right?

546
30:18.988 --> 30:19.923
Huh?

547
30:19.989 --> 30:21.424
Search team to base.

548
30:21.491 --> 30:24.928
We found an aluminum blanket that could have belonged to them!

549
30:48.484 --> 30:49.619
He's so fast.

550
31:05.735 --> 31:07.770
Hey! I can't keep up!

551
31:48.478 --> 31:50.546
How did he even find her here…

552
31:56.986 --> 31:59.522
Ms. Saruwatari. Open your eyes!

553
32:00.123 --> 32:00.990
Ms. Saruwatari.

554
32:03.626 --> 32:04.560
Ms. Saruwatari.

555
32:05.628 --> 32:06.829
Ms. Aya!

556
32:12.168 --> 32:14.404
Ms. Aya. Are you okay?

557
32:15.538 --> 32:16.506
Sorry…

558
32:16.572 --> 32:18.574
Don't move her!

559
32:18.641 --> 32:20.476
Ms. Saruwatari, are you okay?

560
32:20.543 --> 32:21.878
-Sorry… -Are you okay?

561
32:21.944 --> 32:24.814
-Ogoma. Is she wet? -Yes.

562
32:24.881 --> 32:27.383
Take off her jacket. Her body temperature is dropping.

563
32:27.984 --> 32:28.818
Okay.

564
32:29.352 --> 32:31.754
Ms. Aya. I'll take your jacket off.

565
32:31.821 --> 32:32.722
Be gentle.

566
32:33.523 --> 32:35.224
Are you okay? I'm taking it off.

567
32:35.291 --> 32:36.793
Wait a moment.

568
32:36.859 --> 32:39.128
Her arm may be broken.

569
32:39.929 --> 32:41.130
Don't force it.

570
32:42.098 --> 32:43.099
Are you okay?

571
32:43.166 --> 32:44.233
Here.

572
32:45.134 --> 32:46.836
-Put it under her arm. -Thank you.

573
32:47.437 --> 32:49.472
-Can I lift your arm a bit? -Be gentle.

574
32:52.141 --> 32:54.143
Search team six to base.

575
32:54.210 --> 32:56.212
We found Ms. Aya Saruwatari.

576
32:56.846 --> 32:58.915
East side of the mountain.

577
32:59.982 --> 33:02.118
540 meters high.

578
33:02.718 --> 33:04.220
Please send rescue.

579
33:05.088 --> 33:06.422
-So cool. -Are you okay?

580
33:06.489 --> 33:08.791
-Give me another heat pack. -Okay, sure.

581
33:09.792 --> 33:13.496
ORIENT DINER

582
33:18.701 --> 33:20.369
Ms. Harune, what happened to the president?

583
33:20.436 --> 33:22.305
He died. He is dead.

584
33:25.708 --> 33:26.576
Harune!

585
33:26.642 --> 33:28.878
If he's dead, what happens to this place?

586
33:28.945 --> 33:30.246
I'll contact you when I find out.

587
33:30.313 --> 33:31.581
The president is dead?

588
33:31.647 --> 33:32.715
Why?

589
33:32.782 --> 33:35.118
I don't know. I want to ask her too.

590
33:35.184 --> 33:37.019
What are we supposed to do now?

591
33:37.086 --> 33:39.255
Why isn't she telling us anything?

592
33:39.322 --> 33:40.923
Hey, explain!

593
33:40.990 --> 33:43.126
I told you, I'll contact when I find out.

594
33:43.192 --> 33:44.994
Really? What do we do now?

595
33:46.796 --> 33:49.899
-What should we do? -Can't you see I'm busy?

596
34:05.281 --> 34:06.549
Ms. Saruwatari.

597
34:07.049 --> 34:08.851
Are you in pain?

598
34:09.719 --> 34:11.053
-Yes. -Any other issues…

599
34:11.120 --> 34:12.989
She's your teacher? From when?

600
34:13.689 --> 34:15.224
Back in middle school.

601
34:15.958 --> 34:17.026
Well…

602
34:17.093 --> 34:19.162
She was just a trainee teacher.

603
34:19.228 --> 34:20.696
And you remember her name?

604
34:21.764 --> 34:23.866
-Yeah. -Amazing.

605
34:25.368 --> 34:27.570
You did well to find her there.

606
34:28.905 --> 34:33.242
At my school, the whole school climbed that mountain for class.

607
34:33.309 --> 34:35.511
We couldn't graduate if we skipped.

608
34:35.578 --> 34:37.246
So you actually climbed it.

609
34:38.481 --> 34:42.618
The trail we used then is damaged now and not used anymore.

610
34:43.619 --> 34:45.588
I figured she might not know that,

611
34:45.655 --> 34:49.292
and might try to use the old trail and go down the ridge.

612
34:49.358 --> 34:53.095
Oh, you still remember your middle school days so well.

613
34:53.162 --> 34:55.765
I only remember studying.

614
34:57.033 --> 34:59.202
I don't want to remember it much.

615
34:59.268 --> 35:00.102
Why?

616
35:01.337 --> 35:03.239
One memory

617
35:04.040 --> 35:06.509
makes everything come back, and it's annoying.

618
35:07.810 --> 35:09.946
My mind gets messed up.

619
35:12.081 --> 35:13.282
Detective.

620
35:13.349 --> 35:14.717
Yes.

621
35:18.054 --> 35:19.288
Here.

622
35:20.289 --> 35:22.558
I won't get in your way.

623
35:23.492 --> 35:24.527
Follow me.

624
35:27.563 --> 35:28.998
-Thank you very much. -Okay.

625
35:30.766 --> 35:32.101
See you later.

626
35:40.676 --> 35:43.479
A police officer wants to talk to you.

627
35:43.546 --> 35:45.815
This is the detective who found you.

628
35:47.817 --> 35:48.818
20 HOURS LEFT

629
35:48.884 --> 35:50.019
Please come in.

630
35:51.854 --> 35:55.191
Her left arm is broken. She's on painkillers.

631
35:55.891 --> 35:57.260
Please keep it short.

632
35:57.326 --> 35:58.261
Yes.

633
36:01.430 --> 36:03.332
Excuse me. I'm from the Shikara--

634
36:03.399 --> 36:04.667
I'm sorry

635
36:06.035 --> 36:07.503
for the trouble.

636
36:13.743 --> 36:16.979
Is your pain a little better now?

637
36:17.947 --> 36:18.781
Yes.

638
36:20.082 --> 36:24.220
The doctor says once I recover a bit, I'll have surgery.

639
36:24.754 --> 36:25.588
Okay.

640
36:25.655 --> 36:27.123
I heard Ms. Tabatake

641
36:28.090 --> 36:30.393
is in the ICU.

642
36:31.494 --> 36:32.928
What about Mr. Nikaido?

643
36:34.096 --> 36:36.565
We found him. But unfortunately…

644
36:41.003 --> 36:43.673
The others haven't been found yet.

645
36:45.741 --> 36:47.510
Were you all friends?

646
36:48.644 --> 36:49.612
No.

647
36:50.780 --> 36:52.381
We had just met.

648
36:52.448 --> 36:56.652
Can you tell me what happened?

649
37:00.990 --> 37:02.758
Did you take any photos?

650
37:08.831 --> 37:10.333
Do you remember their names?

651
37:11.867 --> 37:13.302
Ms. Tabatake.

652
37:13.369 --> 37:14.337
Yes.

653
37:15.137 --> 37:16.138
Mr. Monden.

654
37:16.205 --> 37:18.474
-Are you tired? You okay? -I'm fine.

655
37:18.541 --> 37:19.842
His wife, Misaki.

656
37:19.909 --> 37:20.910
It's getting cold.

657
37:20.976 --> 37:22.378
Mr. Uematsu.

658
37:24.347 --> 37:26.916
600 yen for a rice ball is too expensive!

659
37:27.616 --> 37:29.051
And water too.

660
37:29.118 --> 37:31.053
-That will be 200 yen. -What?!

661
37:37.993 --> 37:39.195
Mr. Nikaido.

662
37:41.530 --> 37:42.832
Excuse me.

663
37:44.533 --> 37:47.870
May I send some of these photos to the response office?

664
37:47.937 --> 37:50.573
The search is still ongoing.

665
37:51.574 --> 37:52.575
Yes, please.

666
37:53.743 --> 37:55.678
Thank you for your help.

667
37:58.881 --> 38:01.350
Looks like it was nice weather on the way up.

668
38:03.486 --> 38:04.487
Yes.

669
38:06.989 --> 38:10.659
When we started going down, lightning started coming down.

670
38:13.396 --> 38:15.464
The lightning is getting closer.

671
38:15.531 --> 38:17.266
Let's find a safe place to wait this out.

672
38:19.668 --> 38:23.672
Ms. Tabatake said, "Let's rest until the storm passes."

673
38:26.809 --> 38:28.544
It's cold.

674
38:28.611 --> 38:30.079
I have a heat pack.

675
38:30.146 --> 38:32.214
Mr. Nikaido looks lightly dressed.

676
38:32.281 --> 38:35.050
Mr. Nikaido. Please use this.

677
38:35.117 --> 38:36.318
I don't need it.

678
38:36.385 --> 38:38.454
Then it started to rain.

679
38:38.521 --> 38:42.324
He looked cold, and his face was pale.

680
38:42.391 --> 38:44.393
How were the others?

681
38:45.161 --> 38:46.996
Did they seem used to mountains?

682
38:49.331 --> 38:52.201
They seemed used to it.

683
38:55.738 --> 38:59.675
Even with experience, you still decided to hire a guide?

684
39:02.545 --> 39:07.116
Ms. Tabatake knows mountain plants very well.

685
39:08.417 --> 39:11.086
I wanted to see the flowers of this season,

686
39:11.153 --> 39:12.521
so I joined.

687
39:16.158 --> 39:17.827
So you like flowers.

688
39:19.662 --> 39:24.166
I started hiking because I was interested in plants.

689
39:28.604 --> 39:29.538
But…

690
39:32.808 --> 39:34.877
That was the scariest thing

691
39:36.679 --> 39:38.180
that ever happened to me.

692
39:41.884 --> 39:44.553
Mr. Monden! Misaki!

693
39:45.287 --> 39:48.090
Mr. Uematsu! Are you hurt?

694
39:48.757 --> 39:50.259
I'm okay!

695
39:50.326 --> 39:51.560
I'm okay!

696
39:51.627 --> 39:52.595
Calm down!

697
39:53.295 --> 39:55.798
Stay calm and don't move!

698
39:56.365 --> 39:57.466
Yes!

699
39:57.533 --> 40:01.370
We'll wait here until the storm stops.

700
40:01.437 --> 40:03.906
-Are you okay? -I'm going home.

701
40:03.973 --> 40:05.174
Don't move!

702
40:05.741 --> 40:07.476
I'm cold. A bath…

703
40:08.010 --> 40:10.079
-Mr. Nikaido! -I want to take a bath…

704
40:10.713 --> 40:13.315
-Mr. Nikaido! -Do you understand the situation?

705
40:13.382 --> 40:14.817
You could die!

706
40:14.884 --> 40:17.052
Mr. Nikaido, it's dangerous!

707
40:17.119 --> 40:18.888
Are you all right?

708
40:21.824 --> 40:23.225
I'll go bring him back.

709
40:23.292 --> 40:24.760
No, I will.

710
40:25.494 --> 40:27.863
Everyone, please don't move for a while.

711
40:29.031 --> 40:30.065
A heat pack.

712
40:30.799 --> 40:32.101
Thank you.

713
40:33.736 --> 40:36.238
After we couldn't hear the thunder anymore,

714
40:37.206 --> 40:39.308
neither Mr. Nikaido nor Ms. Tabatake

715
40:40.276 --> 40:41.777
came back.

716
40:45.214 --> 40:46.682
What time was it?

717
40:48.183 --> 40:51.520
Around 3:00 p.m.

718
40:52.488 --> 40:54.590
It was getting cold in the mountains.

719
40:56.725 --> 41:01.163
The way back to the trail was blocked by fallen trees.

720
41:01.230 --> 41:02.264
You okay?

721
41:02.331 --> 41:06.468
I didn't know how to lead them down.

722
41:07.903 --> 41:08.938
I…

723
41:09.004 --> 41:11.173
will go down and call for help.

724
41:11.240 --> 41:13.042
No, don't push yourself!

725
41:13.108 --> 41:16.545
As soon as I get a phone signal, I'll call for rescue.

726
41:16.612 --> 41:17.846
Please wait here.

727
41:17.913 --> 41:18.781
Ms. Saruwatari!

728
41:18.847 --> 41:20.215
Will she be okay?

729
41:20.282 --> 41:21.617
While going down,

730
41:22.384 --> 41:24.553
I thought I heard a scream.

731
41:25.220 --> 41:26.088
So…

732
41:26.922 --> 41:28.490
I went toward the stream.

733
41:32.361 --> 41:33.429
Ms. Tabatake!

734
41:34.096 --> 41:35.531
Where are you?

735
41:35.598 --> 41:37.466
Please answer me.

736
41:38.534 --> 41:40.169
Mr. Nikaido!

737
41:41.704 --> 41:44.073
I made the wrong choice.

738
41:45.107 --> 41:48.611
I should have gone straight down and called for help.

739
41:50.212 --> 41:54.049
No one can think clearly in a situation like that.

740
41:54.917 --> 41:58.988
It's my fault we were late going down.

741
42:00.389 --> 42:01.991
I wanted to see flowers,

742
42:03.092 --> 42:04.960
so I stopped everyone many times.

743
42:05.561 --> 42:11.400
The others didn't care about flowers at all.

744
42:19.441 --> 42:20.776
Ms. Saruwatari.

745
42:27.616 --> 42:31.086
I'm glad you're safe.

746
42:36.325 --> 42:39.395
We will find the others.

747
42:46.001 --> 42:50.606
If you remember anything that could help the search,

748
42:51.440 --> 42:53.942
please contact me.

749
43:06.989 --> 43:07.990
Ogoma?

750
43:12.995 --> 43:14.196
Ogoma!

751
43:25.274 --> 43:27.443
Ogoma, are you okay?

752
43:28.177 --> 43:29.344
What's wrong?

753
43:30.813 --> 43:31.980
All right.

754
43:32.581 --> 43:33.916
It's okay.

755
43:35.184 --> 43:36.819
It's okay.

756
43:37.786 --> 43:39.722
I'm here.

757
43:40.289 --> 43:41.724
It's okay.

758
43:43.325 --> 43:44.426
Yes.

759
43:48.263 --> 43:49.465
You…

760
43:50.365 --> 43:52.167
You really are Ogoma.

761
43:53.168 --> 43:55.304
Hey, Ogoma, you okay?

762
43:55.938 --> 43:57.673
We have water. Want some?

763
43:57.740 --> 43:59.007
What's up, Ogoma?

764
43:59.074 --> 44:00.275
You okay?

765
44:00.342 --> 44:01.677
Want me to head down with you?

766
44:01.744 --> 44:03.946
-Yeah. -Thanks.

767
44:06.315 --> 44:07.449
Thank you.

768
44:09.118 --> 44:11.220
You saved my life.

769
44:13.689 --> 44:14.790
It's nothing.

770
44:16.425 --> 44:17.559
Thank you.

771
44:20.662 --> 44:21.730
Yeah.

772
44:35.577 --> 44:37.312
-Thank you. -Okay, take care.

773
44:38.814 --> 44:40.182
Take care.

774
44:40.249 --> 44:41.617
Take care.

775
44:44.019 --> 44:45.220
Thank you.

776
44:45.287 --> 44:46.155
Come in.

777
44:47.055 --> 44:48.624
Excuse me.

778
44:49.191 --> 44:50.392
I am…

779
44:51.093 --> 44:53.462
Nao from Zennichi Insurance Research.

780
44:54.429 --> 44:57.166
-I heard you wanted to discuss a disease? -Yes.

781
44:57.800 --> 45:00.235
-Have a seat. -Oh, excuse me.

782
45:00.769 --> 45:04.439
I would like to learn about ECO deficiency,

783
45:04.506 --> 45:06.975
a designated incurable disease.

784
45:07.042 --> 45:10.612
-Sorry to bother you when you're busy. -It's no problem.

785
45:10.679 --> 45:15.017
Dr. Yoshino, you know this disease very well, right?

786
45:15.751 --> 45:17.953
I'm not a specialist.

787
45:18.487 --> 45:20.489
I see.

788
45:21.757 --> 45:25.360
I heard it's a very rare disease.

789
45:25.427 --> 45:26.595
Mommy!

790
45:27.429 --> 45:28.697
Mommy!

791
45:32.568 --> 45:33.869
Mommy!

792
45:35.070 --> 45:36.371
Mommy!

793
45:39.374 --> 45:40.576
SIX HOURS LEFT

794
45:41.610 --> 45:43.412
Please start a record.

795
45:43.478 --> 45:44.813
-Yes. -Mr. Teruyuki Nikaido.

796
45:44.880 --> 45:47.282
Date of birth is December 3, 1981.

797
45:47.349 --> 45:49.318
-Excuse me. -44 years old.

798
45:49.384 --> 45:52.487
He has no major medical history or illness.

799
45:52.554 --> 45:56.892
We think a fall is the most likely cause, but we will look at other possibilities.

800
45:56.959 --> 45:58.026
Let's begin.

801
45:58.093 --> 45:59.061
-Please do. -Yes.

802
45:59.127 --> 46:00.429
Hello.

803
46:04.633 --> 46:05.767
What are the autopsy results?

804
46:05.834 --> 46:08.403
The cause of death is a brain injury from a head wound.

805
46:08.470 --> 46:10.739
Maybe he lost consciousness and fell.

806
46:10.806 --> 46:13.108
That's what they told me.

807
46:13.175 --> 46:15.510
So it was just as it looked, right?

808
46:15.577 --> 46:17.379
-The blood test results are-- -Ogoma!

809
46:17.446 --> 46:18.647
-Come here. -I'll call back.

810
46:18.714 --> 46:23.118
Zolpidem was found in Mr. Nikaido's blood.

811
46:23.185 --> 46:25.020
-Zolpidem? -A sleeping pill.

812
46:25.921 --> 46:26.822
Huh?

813
46:26.889 --> 46:29.491
Mr. Nikaido doesn't take any regular medicine, right?

814
46:30.592 --> 46:32.461
That's what his wife said.

815
46:33.462 --> 46:34.930
How much was in his blood?

816
46:34.997 --> 46:37.299
About 1.5 times the normal dose.

817
46:37.366 --> 46:42.437
After taking it, a person gets confused and dizzy in 15 to 30 minutes.

818
46:42.504 --> 46:44.006
30 minutes.

819
46:44.773 --> 46:47.042
You wouldn't take that in the mountains.

820
46:47.109 --> 46:49.778
Did he take a sleeping pill while hiking?

821
46:50.812 --> 46:51.947
Think for yourself.

822
46:56.385 --> 46:58.086
Let's talk to his wife.

823
46:58.654 --> 47:00.856
Any possibility Mr. Nikaido was murdered?

824
47:00.923 --> 47:02.557
I think it had to be an accident.

825
47:03.592 --> 47:06.028
The tour guest we found yesterday

826
47:06.595 --> 47:09.231
said he went down the mountain alone, on his own decision.

827
47:09.298 --> 47:11.533
Alone? No companion?

828
47:11.600 --> 47:14.169
The guide went after him.

829
47:14.736 --> 47:18.740
But from where they were found, they probably went separately.

830
47:21.009 --> 47:22.177
Look into it more.

831
47:22.244 --> 47:23.578
Why?

832
47:23.645 --> 47:27.182
I confirmed the hiking insurance the tour guests had.

833
47:27.849 --> 47:30.419
All five had insurance.

834
47:32.554 --> 47:33.655
How much?

835
47:33.722 --> 47:34.856
Five million yen.

836
47:37.259 --> 47:40.495
Is Mr. Nikaido's hiking insurance paid to his wife?

837
47:41.997 --> 47:43.865
You would think that, wouldn't you?

838
47:44.733 --> 47:45.667
What?

839
47:45.734 --> 47:48.070
If not her, then who is it paid to?

840
48:06.621 --> 48:07.889
Sleeping pills?

841
48:08.590 --> 48:11.660
It wasn't in your husband's prescription history.

842
48:12.561 --> 48:15.263
Do you take sleeping pills?

843
48:15.330 --> 48:16.465
No.

844
48:17.199 --> 48:20.002
I can sleep fine without them.

845
48:22.871 --> 48:24.539
Isn't it strange?

846
48:25.574 --> 48:30.812
Why would he take a sleeping pill in the middle of hiking?

847
48:31.646 --> 48:36.485
Could he have mistaken it for a headache pill or cold medicine?

848
48:37.552 --> 48:39.287
He hates medicine.

849
48:39.988 --> 48:44.393
Even with a headache or a stomachache, he takes nothing and just sleeps.

850
48:44.459 --> 48:45.794
So he never takes medicine himself.

851
48:45.861 --> 48:46.828
No.

852
48:52.200 --> 48:54.669
When did you last talk to him?

853
48:55.537 --> 48:56.638
That would be…

854
48:58.673 --> 49:01.376
The morning he left.

855
49:01.443 --> 49:02.711
What did you talk about?

856
49:04.980 --> 49:06.415
He was in a bad mood.

857
49:09.151 --> 49:13.789
He said the bathroom drain was clogged, and I should clean it before he got home.

858
49:14.723 --> 49:17.059
Is he always like that?

859
49:18.760 --> 49:19.828
Like what?

860
49:19.895 --> 49:21.229
Bossy.

861
49:23.732 --> 49:24.733
Yes.

862
49:27.335 --> 49:29.538
He has always been like that.

863
49:32.040 --> 49:33.208
That is…

864
49:35.110 --> 49:36.344
normal for us.

865
49:41.783 --> 49:46.121
Did Mr. Teruyuki have anyone who hated him?

866
49:50.025 --> 49:51.226
I don't know.

867
49:52.761 --> 49:55.464
What is this? What do you want to know?

868
49:56.965 --> 50:00.735
Whether someone made him take the sleeping pill or not.

869
50:04.339 --> 50:06.441
Don't ask me that!

870
50:07.342 --> 50:10.545
How would I know? Ask someone else.

871
50:16.485 --> 50:18.086
I feel sick.

872
50:18.687 --> 50:19.554
Huh?

873
50:20.989 --> 50:21.923
Harune…

874
50:21.990 --> 50:23.992
-Where is the restroom? -Over here.

875
50:24.793 --> 50:28.363
-Move. -Harune, we're not done talking.

876
50:28.430 --> 50:29.865
Harune!

877
50:31.933 --> 50:33.135
Waiting is part of the job.

878
50:33.201 --> 50:35.170
-Just leave me be! -Yeah, but…

879
50:43.778 --> 50:46.715
-Yes. -It's Nao. Thanks for the other day.

880
50:46.781 --> 50:48.383
How do you know my number?

881
50:48.450 --> 50:51.853
All five tour guests took out hiking insurance.

882
50:51.920 --> 50:53.622
Thanks for the info.

883
50:54.723 --> 50:56.625
Who do you think gets the money if they die?

884
50:56.691 --> 50:58.059
Their families, right?

885
50:58.126 --> 51:00.162
Usually, yes.

886
51:01.062 --> 51:02.364
I'm working right now.

887
51:02.430 --> 51:06.668
The beneficiary for Mr. Monden, his wife, Mr. Uematsu, and Mr. Nikaido

888
51:07.502 --> 51:09.471
is Aya Saruwatari.

889
51:15.544 --> 51:16.978
OPERATING ROOM

890
51:17.045 --> 51:21.383
Five million yen each and four people. That's twenty million yen.

891
51:21.449 --> 51:23.451
If all four die…

892
51:26.488 --> 51:30.492
Ms. Saruwatari gets twenty million yen.

893
51:34.829 --> 51:35.797
What?

894
51:37.299 --> 51:39.434
That has to be a mistake.

895
51:40.168 --> 51:41.937
Did you talk to Harune?

896
51:42.003 --> 51:44.539
She said she felt sick again.

897
51:44.606 --> 51:45.941
Maybe it's an act.

898
51:46.007 --> 51:47.008
Maybe.

899
51:47.075 --> 51:47.909
Ogoma.

900
51:47.976 --> 51:49.911
This isn't just a missing person case.

901
51:51.213 --> 51:53.181
It's a crime, not an accident.

902
51:55.050 --> 51:56.851
At least, that's what I think.

903
52:02.023 --> 52:03.258
Mommy!

904
52:12.467 --> 52:15.737
You mean insurance murder?

905
52:22.177 --> 52:23.645
Am I a suspect now?

906
52:23.712 --> 52:27.148
Either Ms. Tabatake or Ms. Aya is the accomplice.

907
52:27.215 --> 52:28.950
I may have been wrong.

908
52:29.017 --> 52:29.951
Ogoma!

909
52:30.018 --> 52:31.019
Please send backup.

910
52:31.086 --> 52:32.053
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
